# Git attributes: line endings and binary handling.
#
# Without this, Git for Windows (core.autocrlf=true, its default) rewrites LF -> CRLF in
# text files on checkout. For data/ that changes the bytes, so the published SHA-256
# checksums in data/SHA256SUMS would no longer match and tests/test_data_integrity.py
# would fail on every Windows clone. data/ is therefore stored and checked out verbatim.

* text=auto eol=lf

data/**     -text -diff
*.pkl       binary
*.png       binary
*.zip       binary
